# FoodLens AI - environment template
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Restart `npm start` after editing it: EXPO_PUBLIC_*
# values are inlined into the JavaScript bundle at build time.
#
# ============================================================================
# CLIENT values - these SHIP INSIDE THE APP and anyone can read them
# ============================================================================
#
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys
#
# Use the PUBLISHABLE key (`sb_publishable_...`). It is designed to be public:
# on its own it grants nothing, because every table is protected by Row Level
# Security.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here

# Older projects issue a legacy "anon" key (a JWT starting `eyJ`) instead.
# That still works - set this variable rather than the one above.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign in with Google  (optional)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are OAuth client IDENTIFIERS, not secrets. Google publishes them in
# the app bundle by design and they grant nothing on their own, which is why
# they belong in EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables. The client SECRET does not go here,
# or anywhere in this app - only Supabase needs it.
#
# Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create OAuth client
#
#   Web application   -> paste the id below AND into Supabase
#                        (Authentication -> Providers -> Google), along with
#                        its client secret. This is the audience Supabase
#                        verifies the token against, so it is required even
#                        though the app runs on a phone.
#   iOS               -> bundle id com.foodlensai.app
#   Android           -> package name com.foodlensai.app, plus the SHA-1
#                        of the signing certificate
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=123-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=123-ios.apps.googleusercontent.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=123-android.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign in with Apple  (optional, iOS only)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing goes in this file. It needs, in order:
#
#   1. An Apple Developer account, and Sign In with Apple enabled on the App
#      ID for com.foodlensai.app.
#   2. A Services ID and a key, configured in Supabase under
#      Authentication -> Providers -> Apple.
#   3. On iOS, a development or production build. Apple's own sheet needs
#      a native entitlement and cannot work in Expo Go.
#
# The button is offered on every platform. iOS uses Apple's own sheet when
# the device has one; everywhere else, including Android, it opens Apple's
# web flow in a browser and finishes through the same callback the
# confirmation emails use. Both paths need the Services ID above.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER put a privileged key in an EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A secret key (`sb_secret_...`) or a service-role JWT bypasses Row Level
# Security entirely. In an EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable it would be readable by
# anyone who downloads the app, giving them full read and write access to
# every user's data.
#
# The app detects this: `src/lib/env.ts` classifies the key, refuses to use a
# privileged one, and tells you to rotate it. Do not work around that check.

# ============================================================================
# SERVER secrets - documented here, but NEVER set in this file
# ============================================================================
#
# These live only as Supabase Edge Function secrets. Set them with the CLI:
#
#   npx supabase secrets set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY             Key for photo analysis (Claude).
#                                 Get one at console.anthropic.com.
#   USDA_FDC_API_KEY              USDA FoodData Central key, for the food
#                                 database lookup that is not built yet.
#
#   SUPABASE_URL                  Injected into Edge Functions automatically.
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY     Injected automatically. Never set by hand,
#                                 never ship, never log.
#
# If you ever paste one of these into a file with an EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix,
# treat it as leaked and rotate it immediately.
